[2026-01-30T13:47:10.602Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C5K1Pne3K8YRpRKXFmdZbe","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n     2→\n     3→## REQUIREMENT\n     4→\n     5→# Add cross-view entity linking\n     6→\n     7→## Metadata\n     8→- **Category**: functionality\n     9→- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    10→- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    11→- **Scan Type**: pragmatic_integrator\n    12→- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:32:28 AM\n    13→\n    14→## Description\n    15→When a finding mentions an entity, clicking should navigate to EntitiesView with that entity selected. When a source is cited in a finding, clicking should open SourcesView with that source. Implement via URL state or shared context to enable seamless cross-referencing.\n    16→\n    17→## Reasoning\n    18→Currently users must manually navigate between views and find related items. Cross-linking creates a connected research experience where users can trace findings to sources to entities without losing context.\n    19→\n    20→## Context\n    21→\n    22→**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n    23→\n    24→### Context: Report Views\n    25→\n    26→**Description**: Full-page report views for different sections: overview, findings, sources, analysis, entities, and perspectives. Each view provides deep-dive content for its domain.\n    27→**Related Files**:\n    28→- `src/components/report/views/OverviewView.tsx`\n    29→- `src/components/report/views/FindingsView.tsx`\n    30→- `src/components/report/views/SourcesView.tsx`\n    31→- `src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx`\n    32→- `src/components/report/views/EntitiesView.tsx`\n    33→- `src/components/report/views/PerspectivesView.tsx`\n    34→- `src/components/report/views/index.tsx`\n    35→\n    36→**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n    37→\n    38→## Recommended Skills\n    39→\n    40→Use Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills/` directory for available skills.\n    41→\n    42→## Notes\n    43→\n    44→This requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n    45→\n    46→## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n    47→\n    48→1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n    49→   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n    50→   - title: 2-6 word summary\n    51→   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n    52→\n    53→2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n    54→   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n    55→   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n    56→\n    57→3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n    58→\n    59→Begin implementation now.\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbdddf83-efc9-404e-b6a3-e0a9e67b2ab3","uuid":"bf71de5f-3fbf-49c9-93d0-a237d3d25882","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\idea-6da340ad-add-cross-view-entity-linking.md","content":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Add cross-view entity linking\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: functionality\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: pragmatic_integrator\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:32:28 AM\n\n## Description\nWhen a finding mentions an entity, clicking should navigate to EntitiesView with that entity selected. When a source is cited in a finding, clicking should open SourcesView with that source. Implement via URL state or shared context to enable seamless cross-referencing.\n\n## Reasoning\nCurrently users must manually navigate between views and find related items. Cross-linking creates a connected research experience where users can trace findings to sources to entities without losing context.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Views\n\n**Description**: Full-page report views for different sections: overview, findings, sources, analysis, entities, and perspectives. Each view provides deep-dive content for its domain.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/views/OverviewView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/FindingsView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/SourcesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/EntitiesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/PerspectivesView.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/views/index.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\nUse Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills/` directory for available skills.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n\n3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now.","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
